# Axum

Axum owns server-side HTTP and WebSocket wire behavior: routes, extraction, request scopes, multipart and streaming bodies, OpenAPI, WebSocket controllers, endpoint mounting, protocol framing, and publication. Constructing clients and managing their connections belongs under <GuideRef slug="clients">generated clients</GuideRef>.

## Choose a server task

| Task | Guide |
|---|---|
| define controllers and routes, extract requests, upload multipart data, stream bodies, or publish OpenAPI | <GuideRef slug="axum/http">HTTP</GuideRef> |
| define WebSocket destinations, mount endpoints, author a protocol, or publish typed topics | <GuideRef slug="axum/websocket">WebSocket</GuideRef> |

## Shared prerequisites

Start with the <GuideRef slug="framework">application model</GuideRef>, enable the `axum` facade feature, and add only the optional `multipart`, `openapi`, `ws`, `json-ws`, or `stomp` features required by the selected server surface.
